<title>GREECE: CREDIT AGRICOLE BUYS 10.5PCT OF ASPIS PRONIA.</title>
<headline>CREDIT AGRICOLE BUYS 10.5PCT OF ASPIS PRONIA.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Agricole Lazard Financial Products Bank acquired a 10.53 percent stake in Aspis Pronia through a block trade of 2,403,846 common registered shares at 1,040 drachmas a share, Aspis Pronia said.</p>
<p>The block was put through by Aspis subsidiary Aspis Securities and the block was sold by its major shareholder, president and managing director Pavlos Psomiadis, it said.</p>
